course: dictionary
lesson: 12304
title: Corgi: a small dog with a big job
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A corgi is a small dog with short legs, a long body and pointed ears. Its face looks a bit like a fox's. The word is a noun, so it names a thing: a corgi, or two or more corgis. «Our corgi, Biscuit, has short legs and a long, furry body.» Those clues tell you exactly what a corgi looks like.
explain: The word also tells you what a corgi was made for. Corgis were first bred in Wales to herd cattle, which means to guide cows from place to place. «The corgi ran round the cows and kept them together in the field.» The clue is ran round the cows: the dog is doing a herding job.
explain: Many corgis today are pets rather than working dogs. «My friend's corgi wags its tail every time we visit.» You can read about corgis in stories and news too, because they are famous as the favourite dogs of Queen Elizabeth the Second. Whenever you meet a new dog name, check the words around it for clues.
fact: A corgi is a small dog with short legs and a long body.
fact: Corgis have pointed ears and a face that looks a bit like a fox's.
fact: Corgis were first bred in Wales to herd cattle.
fact: The word «corgi» comes from Welsh.
fact: Corgis are popular pets, and they were the favourite dogs of Queen Elizabeth the Second.
exercise: «The corgi ran round the cows and kept them in one field.» What is a corgi? | A large horse used for pulling carts | A kind of cow that lives in Wales | *A small dog with short legs and pointed ears | A bird that herds sheep
exercise: What language does the word corgi come from? | French | Scots | *Welsh | Latin
exercise: «The corgi has pointed ears and a face like a fox.» Find and copy one word that describes the ears. | face | fox | corgi | *pointed
test: Corgis were first bred in which country to herd cattle? | England | Scotland | Ireland | *Wales
test: «My friend's corgi has short legs and a long, furry body.» Which part of the corgi is long? | Ears | *Body | Legs | Tail
exam: Why were corgis first bred? | To sleep on the Queen's bed | *To herd cattle in Wales | To guard the sea from pirates | To win races at the dog show
